1
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:37,507
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,807 --> 00:02:41,827
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:46,007
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:46,587 --> 00:02:50,887
Maki D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:51,167 --> 00:02:53,647
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:54,027 --> 00:02:56,627
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,927 --> 00:02:59,747
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,747 --> 00:03:02,847
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:04,087 --> 00:03:05,767
Now this sight!

10
00:03:06,747 --> 00:03:09,587
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:10,047 --> 00:03:13,167
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:13,367 --> 00:03:17,447
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:21,587 --> 00:03:26,367
Luffy was sent flying from the Sabaody Archipelago by Bartholomew Kuma.

14
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:28,947
After soaring through the sky for hours,

15
00:03:29,087 --> 00:03:31,927
he found himself in a kingdom inhabited entirely by women.

16
00:03:32,467 --> 00:03:34,527
Captured by the Pirate Empress Hancock,

17
00:03:34,927 --> 00:03:39,327
Luffy was forced into combat with her sisters, Marigold and Sandersonia,

18
00:03:39,627 --> 00:03:42,267
who had both eaten different snake-steak fruits.

19
00:03:42,807 --> 00:03:44,467
Why, of all the insolent...

20
00:03:44,467 --> 00:03:46,987
Mary, this is your chance to finish him off!

21
00:03:47,147 --> 00:03:47,787
I can't.

22
00:03:47,987 --> 00:03:49,067
Don't you understand?

23
00:03:50,067 --> 00:03:51,827
He isn't mocking you, sister.

24
00:03:52,427 --> 00:03:55,527
That man is... protecting us!

25
00:03:55,527 --> 00:03:59,267
You'd rather die than let people see this thing on your back, right?

26
00:03:59,267 --> 00:04:11,187
Hancock's confession.

27
00:04:11,187 --> 00:04:13,607
The sisters abhor it past.

28
00:04:13,607 --> 00:04:43,587
The sisters abhor it past.

29
00:04:43,927 --> 00:04:45,847
Well, is it all clear now?

30
00:04:48,887 --> 00:04:50,467
Are you alright, Sonia?

31
00:04:56,807 --> 00:04:58,607
Please forgive us, Hancock.

32
00:04:58,747 --> 00:05:00,827
We lost and were rescued by our enemy.

33
00:05:02,907 --> 00:05:04,527
Okay, what now?

34
00:05:04,707 --> 00:05:05,267
You next?

35
00:05:05,267 --> 00:05:14,887
We're done.

36
00:05:17,747 --> 00:05:19,447
I'm not in the mood to fight.

37
00:05:20,087 --> 00:05:20,607
Really?

38
00:05:20,607 --> 00:05:22,227
Is she okay?

39
00:05:22,487 --> 00:05:23,087
No cracks?

40
00:05:25,967 --> 00:05:27,967
So, you're gonna fix him, right?

41
00:05:28,247 --> 00:05:29,367
Make him normal again?

42
00:05:32,807 --> 00:05:33,367
What?

43
00:05:33,927 --> 00:05:34,947
You heard me.

44
00:05:35,087 --> 00:05:36,527
You can make him normal, right?

45
00:05:37,267 --> 00:05:38,007
Can't you?

46
00:05:38,007 --> 00:05:39,927
It's not like they did anything wrong!

47
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:41,287
They just told the truth!

48
00:05:41,827 --> 00:05:42,487
Come on!

49
00:05:42,747 --> 00:05:43,067
Please?

50
00:05:47,327 --> 00:05:48,627
Of course I can.

51
00:05:49,007 --> 00:05:52,027
I can easily reverse the effects if I choose to do so.

52
00:05:53,027 --> 00:05:59,047
But, to be clear, didn't you say you wanted to go somewhere by ship?

53
00:05:59,407 --> 00:06:01,587
Yeah, I gotta get back and find my crew!

54
00:06:02,167 --> 00:06:02,687
I see.

55
00:06:03,387 --> 00:06:04,767
I have bad news.

56
00:06:05,007 --> 00:06:05,887
You must decide.

57
00:06:05,887 --> 00:06:10,347
I can either return them to normal, or help you to reach your destination.

58
00:06:11,607 --> 00:06:13,127
Choose one, forget the other.

59
00:06:13,627 --> 00:06:15,167
That's all I'm willing to do.

60
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:18,467
Awful.

61
00:06:18,907 --> 00:06:20,267
Just awful.

62
00:06:21,927 --> 00:06:23,647
You can't fool me.

63
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:26,987
Now we'll see your true nature.

64
00:06:28,007 --> 00:06:28,967
Good deal!

65
00:06:29,167 --> 00:06:29,907
That's great!

66
00:06:31,107 --> 00:06:34,027
Well, okay, go ahead and turn him back!

67
00:06:35,887 --> 00:06:37,747
Seriously!

68
00:06:38,347 --> 00:06:39,327
Thank you!

69
00:06:46,927 --> 00:06:54,907
That man, he has such an immensely powerful hockey, but didn't hesitate to save those he owes.

70
00:06:56,227 --> 00:06:56,827
Incredible.

71
00:06:57,727 --> 00:06:58,327
Sister.

72
00:06:58,887 --> 00:06:59,567
Vixis?

73
00:06:59,567 --> 00:06:59,607
Vixis?

74
00:07:05,887 --> 00:07:31,147
That man defies us, then he risks his life to protect us?

75
00:07:31,147 --> 00:07:32,287
What a weirdo!

76
00:07:32,807 --> 00:07:34,487
There's no question about that.

77
00:07:34,767 --> 00:07:39,327
But unfortunately for him, I doubt his kindness will be enough for the Snake Princess to dismiss

78
00:07:39,327 --> 00:07:40,247
his rude behavior.

79
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:43,087
And it's even more unlikely that she'll forgive the others.

80
00:07:46,607 --> 00:07:47,167
Huh?

81
00:07:47,167 --> 00:07:49,627
Hey, look, it's Margaret!

82
00:07:49,947 --> 00:07:50,567
Sweet Pea!

83
00:07:51,087 --> 00:07:52,007
And a palandra!

84
00:07:52,247 --> 00:07:52,847
Hey, everyone!

85
00:07:53,067 --> 00:07:54,307
I was wondering where you went.

86
00:07:54,407 --> 00:07:55,127
How wonderful!

87
00:07:55,287 --> 00:07:56,527
She reversed the petrification!

88
00:07:57,607 --> 00:07:58,727
I was so worried!

89
00:07:59,067 --> 00:08:01,467
I just couldn't believe it when you defended that man!

90
00:08:01,907 --> 00:08:02,727
None of us could.

91
00:08:03,167 --> 00:08:04,467
And then you were turned to stone.

92
00:08:04,627 --> 00:08:05,247
It was awful!

93
00:08:05,587 --> 00:08:05,987
Stone?

94
00:08:06,407 --> 00:08:06,707
Huh?

95
00:08:07,667 --> 00:08:08,167
Uh...

96
00:08:08,167 --> 00:08:10,387
What happened to us?

97
00:08:10,847 --> 00:08:11,907
Most peculiar.

98
00:08:12,287 --> 00:08:13,687
I have no recollection.

99
00:08:14,207 --> 00:08:15,667
You can't remember a thing?

100
00:08:15,747 --> 00:08:15,967
No.

101
00:08:16,627 --> 00:08:19,967
I came to, and the man, well, he seemed so happy.

102
00:08:20,687 --> 00:08:21,067
Ugh!

103
00:08:21,487 --> 00:08:22,287
This is great!

104
00:08:22,907 --> 00:08:24,467
I was really freaking out there!

105
00:08:24,507 --> 00:08:26,087
I thought you guys were gonna die!

106
00:08:26,847 --> 00:08:28,487
Where did everyone go?

107
00:08:28,627 --> 00:08:29,727
Is the trial over?

108
00:08:30,307 --> 00:08:31,347
Oh, hey, lady!

109
00:08:31,527 --> 00:08:32,007
Thanks!

110
00:08:32,007 --> 00:08:32,407
Huh?

111
00:08:34,007 --> 00:08:34,927
Snake Princess!

112
00:08:35,667 --> 00:08:36,007
We...

113
00:08:37,147 --> 00:08:38,007
Um...

114
00:08:38,007 --> 00:08:42,907
Continue to dedicate yourselves to the protection of our nation.

115
00:08:51,247 --> 00:08:52,747
That's all I can remember.

116
00:08:53,287 --> 00:08:54,207
It's fine!

117
00:08:54,427 --> 00:08:57,527
You're not the first to have trouble remembering after you've been turned to stone.

118
00:08:57,807 --> 00:09:00,447
Don't worry, I'll catch you up on the details of what happened later.

119
00:09:00,747 --> 00:09:01,887
But what did happen?

120
00:09:02,187 --> 00:09:03,687
And what did she do with the man?

121
00:09:04,227 --> 00:09:05,487
You really need to ask?

122
00:09:05,487 --> 00:09:07,787
She just turned him to stone and got on with her day.

123
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:09,427
Sa-sa-sa-sa!

124
00:09:09,807 --> 00:09:14,107
Well, I could be mistaken, but it looked like they took him to Kuja Castle.

125
00:09:14,327 --> 00:09:14,727
What?

126
00:09:18,687 --> 00:09:20,827
Hey, what'd you say you want from me?

127
00:09:21,207 --> 00:09:25,147
Oh, please tell me you're gonna serve up a big after-battle meal for us?

128
00:09:26,747 --> 00:09:29,587
We're gonna get along just fine if that's what it is.

129
00:09:29,887 --> 00:09:32,187
So, what's the best food around here?

130
00:09:32,347 --> 00:09:33,307
Some kind of meat?

131
00:09:33,987 --> 00:09:36,407
Just so you know, I'm grateful for what you did.

132
00:09:36,947 --> 00:09:37,507
Thank you.

133
00:09:38,047 --> 00:09:39,707
Forget it, it was nothing, really.

134
00:09:39,947 --> 00:09:41,247
Feed me and we'll call it even.

135
00:09:41,367 --> 00:09:43,147
If anyone had seen what's on our backs,

136
00:09:43,407 --> 00:09:44,727
it would have been the end of us.

137
00:09:45,007 --> 00:09:47,167
We'd be cast out, never to return.

138
00:09:47,907 --> 00:09:48,687
You may enter.

139
00:09:50,387 --> 00:09:52,087
I said come inside.

140
00:09:52,707 --> 00:09:53,107
Where?

141
00:09:54,067 --> 00:09:55,127
Behind the curtain.

142
00:09:55,547 --> 00:09:57,467
Oh, you got the food back there?

143
00:09:57,947 --> 00:09:58,947
Here I come!

144
00:09:59,587 --> 00:10:01,207
Hey, where's the food?

145
00:10:02,067 --> 00:10:04,447
And how come you took your clothes off?

146
00:10:04,967 --> 00:10:07,367
My, astute and charming, aren't you?

147
00:10:08,627 --> 00:10:09,307
Look.

148
00:10:26,987 --> 00:10:28,527
The mark on my back.

149
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:31,207
You, you said...

150
00:10:31,207 --> 00:10:34,967
You said that you'd seen it before.

151
00:10:36,507 --> 00:10:37,507
I need to know.

152
00:10:37,927 --> 00:10:38,847
Take a closer look.

153
00:10:41,507 --> 00:10:42,647
Where have you seen it?

154
00:10:43,287 --> 00:10:45,127
Do you know what this mark means?

155
00:10:45,127 --> 00:10:55,167
Answer me.

156
00:10:55,167 --> 00:10:56,127
Hurry up.

157
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:59,007
This isn't pleasant, you know.

158
00:11:05,647 --> 00:11:09,447
It's not the same, but it still reminds me of the one I've seen before.

159
00:11:09,447 --> 00:11:10,567
There's this friend of mine.

160
00:11:10,567 --> 00:11:11,567
There's this friend of mine.

161
00:11:11,567 --> 00:11:13,627
He's a fish man, and his name is Hachi.

162
00:11:14,487 --> 00:11:15,367
A fish man?

163
00:11:15,507 --> 00:11:15,847
Yeah.

164
00:11:16,107 --> 00:11:19,467
He's got a mark kind of like that one on his forehead, but it's different.

165
00:11:19,947 --> 00:11:21,567
I've never seen one like yours.

166
00:11:22,327 --> 00:11:24,847
If he doesn't know what it is, tell him.

167
00:11:25,547 --> 00:11:26,067
Granny, you...

168
00:11:26,067 --> 00:11:27,787
Why are you here?

169
00:11:27,927 --> 00:11:29,547
Snake Princess, be honest.

170
00:11:29,967 --> 00:11:31,927
You know you can trust him by now.

171
00:11:31,927 --> 00:11:34,607
You've seen with your own eyes he's a good man.

172
00:11:36,547 --> 00:11:37,627
Go ahead, child.

173
00:11:38,087 --> 00:11:39,167
Do not fear.

174
00:11:39,427 --> 00:11:40,747
Your secret is safe.

175
00:11:43,767 --> 00:11:44,347
You.

176
00:11:44,587 --> 00:11:48,007
You're the notorious pirate known as Monkey D. Luffy, correct?

177
00:11:48,647 --> 00:11:49,627
Yeah, that's me.

178
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:52,007
But how do you know anything about me?

179
00:11:52,267 --> 00:11:56,547
You do seem like a decent enough young man, despite your reputation.

180
00:11:56,547 --> 00:11:58,667
Take a look at this newspaper.

181
00:11:59,167 --> 00:12:04,927
Just a few days before he arrived, he caused an incident on the Sabaori Archipelago.

182
00:12:05,327 --> 00:12:07,527
An incident with dire repercussions.

183
00:12:07,847 --> 00:12:12,427
Not only did he oppose the Celestial Dragons, he punched one of them.

184
00:12:15,847 --> 00:12:18,207
You must be insane.

185
00:12:18,207 --> 00:12:27,627
By some miracle, he was able to escape the Central Forces they unleashed to capture him.

186
00:12:28,447 --> 00:12:34,887
And just as miraculous, he traveled from that faraway location to here in a few short days.

187
00:12:35,287 --> 00:12:38,207
Both of these things are beyond my comprehension.

188
00:12:39,067 --> 00:12:41,147
No, that's impossible.

189
00:12:41,547 --> 00:12:42,447
I told you.

190
00:12:42,647 --> 00:12:43,067
Remember?

191
00:12:43,347 --> 00:12:44,327
I got flung here.

192
00:12:44,647 --> 00:12:46,627
Honestly, I don't even know where we are.

193
00:12:46,787 --> 00:12:47,707
I've never heard of it.

194
00:12:48,827 --> 00:12:52,987
And I don't feel one bit bad about knocking out that Celestial Dragon.

195
00:12:53,627 --> 00:12:56,967
Does that newspaper even mention what that bastard did to my friend?

196
00:12:57,847 --> 00:12:59,327
Then it's true?

197
00:13:00,087 --> 00:13:03,367
Are you telling me that you actually struck a Celestial Dragon?

198
00:13:06,667 --> 00:13:07,727
I'm amazed.

199
00:13:09,007 --> 00:13:10,727
I truly had no idea.

200
00:13:10,727 --> 00:13:20,747
That there could be such a wonderful fool left in this world.

201
00:13:25,827 --> 00:13:29,107
To challenge the world nobles and risk your life?

202
00:13:31,647 --> 00:13:33,307
You're just like he was.

203
00:13:33,307 --> 00:14:02,087
I will tell you everything there is to know.

204
00:14:02,087 --> 00:14:05,567
I can even tell you why your fishman friend has that emblem.

205
00:14:06,187 --> 00:14:07,787
And also what it means.

206
00:14:08,787 --> 00:14:09,567
Paji's mark.

207
00:14:12,047 --> 00:14:13,707
This brand is...

208
00:14:13,707 --> 00:14:18,487
The claw of the Celestial Dragon.

209
00:14:18,487 --> 00:14:21,987
The emblem of the world nobles.

210
00:14:21,987 --> 00:14:34,267
The Celestial Dragons branded upon those they take as slaves.

211
00:14:35,407 --> 00:14:38,607
A marking to steal your humanity and claim you as their property.

212
00:14:38,607 --> 00:14:40,467
And they marked you?

213
00:14:43,387 --> 00:14:44,027
You see?

214
00:14:44,307 --> 00:14:45,387
The three of us were...

215
00:14:45,387 --> 00:14:48,387
My sisters and I...

216
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:57,167
We were once slaves...

217
00:14:57,167 --> 00:14:58,447
Of the world nobles.

218
00:14:58,447 --> 00:14:59,087
Uh...

219
00:14:59,087 --> 00:15:15,387
You guys were...

220
00:15:15,387 --> 00:15:16,747
Their slaves?

221
00:15:16,747 --> 00:15:29,027
It happened when I was 12 years old.

222
00:15:33,027 --> 00:15:35,427
Okay! Starbird! Clear!

223
00:15:35,867 --> 00:15:37,807
Same here! Port all clear, too!

224
00:15:38,567 --> 00:15:39,787
Bow! All clear!

225
00:15:40,647 --> 00:15:43,027
And visibility is high. All is calm.

226
00:15:43,367 --> 00:15:44,847
Careful you don't fall in the ocean!

227
00:15:46,747 --> 00:15:50,827
Don't make fun of me. Geez, I'm a warrior now, aren't I?

228
00:15:51,247 --> 00:15:53,827
Yeah, yeah. Don't worry, we trust you.

229
00:15:55,647 --> 00:15:57,327
You tell him, Big Big!

230
00:15:57,407 --> 00:15:58,647
You know we believe in you!

231
00:15:59,467 --> 00:16:02,147
You hungry? I brought a snack out for you.

232
00:16:03,207 --> 00:16:04,347
Hey, Hancock!

233
00:16:04,707 --> 00:16:06,967
Sonia! Mary! Where are you?

234
00:16:06,967 --> 00:16:10,167
The three of us were abducted from a Kuja pirate ship.

235
00:16:10,487 --> 00:16:11,927
In broad daylight, no less.

236
00:16:13,787 --> 00:16:15,447
And then we were sold.

237
00:16:16,747 --> 00:16:24,347
From that point on, we were submitted to a hell we can never forget.

238
00:16:24,347 --> 00:16:45,787
The first men we ever encountered were nothing but figures of cruelty and horror.

239
00:16:45,787 --> 00:16:51,087
Sonia! It'll be okay!

240
00:16:51,747 --> 00:16:54,087
The memories will always haunt us.

241
00:16:54,787 --> 00:16:57,547
Hey, don't put yourself through this! I've heard enough!

242
00:16:57,747 --> 00:16:59,467
Really! Please, don't keep going!

243
00:16:59,507 --> 00:17:00,507
It was all so awful.

244
00:17:01,087 --> 00:17:02,787
Our world was naught but despair.

245
00:17:03,367 --> 00:17:04,967
And we prayed for the mercy of death.

246
00:17:05,067 --> 00:17:06,787
Hey, come on!

247
00:17:06,787 --> 00:17:07,787
We'll be right back.

248
00:17:07,867 --> 00:17:08,547
We'll be right back.

249
00:17:08,547 --> 00:17:12,087
But, after four years of that misery,

250
00:17:12,607 --> 00:17:16,227
there came a night that shocked even the world government to its core.

251
00:17:18,147 --> 00:17:20,047
It was accepted as a rule of the world

252
00:17:20,047 --> 00:17:23,207
that no one would ever dare challenge the Celestial Dragons.

253
00:17:23,867 --> 00:17:25,227
But on that fateful night,

254
00:17:25,587 --> 00:17:28,827
there was a man who scaled the red line with his bare hands

255
00:17:28,827 --> 00:17:30,247
and slipped into Marijua,

256
00:17:30,587 --> 00:17:32,507
the holy land of the Celestial Dragons.

257
00:17:38,627 --> 00:17:43,167
This man was an adventurer who later led the fishman pirates,

258
00:17:43,547 --> 00:17:44,347
Fisher Tiger.

259
00:17:45,227 --> 00:17:48,427
He arrived with the sole purpose of releasing his fellow fishmen

260
00:17:48,427 --> 00:17:49,527
who suffered as slaves.

261
00:17:49,967 --> 00:17:52,547
He wreaked havoc on the world nobles without reserve.

262
00:17:52,547 --> 00:17:58,707
Despite his hatred for humans as a species,

263
00:17:59,327 --> 00:18:00,967
he freed every one of us,

264
00:18:01,367 --> 00:18:04,627
saving thousands of slaves regardless of who or what they were.

265
00:18:06,087 --> 00:18:07,467
And so we fled,

266
00:18:07,827 --> 00:18:09,467
more than willing to risk death.

267
00:18:14,347 --> 00:18:15,227
I know!

268
00:18:22,547 --> 00:18:27,507
We owe an eternal debt to Fisher Tiger.

269
00:18:31,007 --> 00:18:32,107
In the end,

270
00:18:32,507 --> 00:18:33,787
Tiger unleashed an army.

271
00:18:34,207 --> 00:18:35,647
Fishmen swarmed the oceans.

272
00:18:36,667 --> 00:18:40,007
But they were cursed to wear the Celestial Dragons' mark of slavery.

273
00:18:41,387 --> 00:18:44,327
Tiger was relentlessly hunted by the world government,

274
00:18:44,587 --> 00:18:47,987
so he brought the fugitives together to form the Pirates of the Sun

275
00:18:47,987 --> 00:18:50,927
and sailed far and wide across the seas.

276
00:18:50,927 --> 00:18:56,067
In order to erase the last trace of their bondage,

277
00:18:56,487 --> 00:19:00,587
the former slaves made a new brand over the claw of the Celestial Dragon,

278
00:19:01,967 --> 00:19:05,227
changing them into a symbol of the Sun.

279
00:19:06,387 --> 00:19:07,567
There you have it.

280
00:19:08,027 --> 00:19:11,147
By necessity, my brand bears a similarity in design.

281
00:19:11,527 --> 00:19:14,627
That's why you mistook it for the symbol of the Sun pirates before.

282
00:19:15,007 --> 00:19:16,347
Yeah, guess so.

283
00:19:16,747 --> 00:19:19,487
The mark on Hachi's forehead does look like a sun.

284
00:19:19,487 --> 00:19:23,367
Wait, does that mean Hachi used to be a slave?

285
00:19:23,747 --> 00:19:25,767
Possibly, although not necessarily.

286
00:19:26,487 --> 00:19:28,787
Not all of Tiger's pirates were former slaves,

287
00:19:28,927 --> 00:19:32,007
but they were all branded with the symbol to hide their comrades' past,

288
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:34,227
which is why, former slave or not,

289
00:19:34,287 --> 00:19:38,287
it's safe to assume that your friend must have sailed with the Sun pirates at some point.

290
00:19:39,047 --> 00:19:41,787
Fisher Tiger has been dead for some time now.

291
00:19:41,787 --> 00:19:46,787
Upon his passing, the Sun pirates disbanded and split into several factions.

292
00:19:50,627 --> 00:19:51,427
Hold on.

293
00:19:51,907 --> 00:19:53,367
Where did you get that wound on your head?

294
00:19:53,367 --> 00:19:54,547
Huh? Oh, that.

295
00:19:54,927 --> 00:19:56,227
Don't worry about it, okay?

296
00:19:56,847 --> 00:19:59,547
I knew we had a pretty dark past, but geez.

297
00:20:00,047 --> 00:20:02,027
Now that you know the history of the mark,

298
00:20:02,167 --> 00:20:04,267
I hope you can better understand our position.

299
00:20:04,267 --> 00:20:07,807
Yeah, I think I get it.

300
00:20:08,487 --> 00:20:08,947
It's sick.

301
00:20:09,367 --> 00:20:11,387
The things that they made us do as slaves.

302
00:20:11,967 --> 00:20:13,887
They forced me to eat the love-love fruit,

303
00:20:14,127 --> 00:20:17,327
and forced my sisters to eat snake-snake fruits for their amusement.

304
00:20:18,067 --> 00:20:21,427
Ironically, this allowed us to hide our secret from the Kuja.

305
00:20:21,427 --> 00:20:26,127
They praise our powers because they misunderstand them.

306
00:20:26,787 --> 00:20:29,507
But if you hadn't covered Sandersonia's back in the arena,

307
00:20:29,967 --> 00:20:31,987
the ugly truth would be apparent to them.

308
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:39,207
I can't stand for anyone to know of our past.

309
00:20:45,587 --> 00:20:48,627
And I shall make any sacrifice to ensure that.

310
00:20:51,427 --> 00:20:56,987
Even if I must deceive my own people,

311
00:20:57,287 --> 00:21:00,187
I won't let anyone control us again!

312
00:21:03,367 --> 00:21:05,327
I fear my own subjects.

313
00:21:05,747 --> 00:21:07,827
I can't let anyone come close to me,

314
00:21:07,847 --> 00:21:09,047
or they might know the truth.

315
00:21:13,567 --> 00:21:14,167
Sister!

316
00:21:14,167 --> 00:21:19,247
Well, on the bright side of things,

317
00:21:19,247 --> 00:21:21,447
it's been years since you've displayed

318
00:21:21,447 --> 00:21:24,387
even the most faint affectation of an emotion.

319
00:21:24,667 --> 00:21:25,987
But I welcome your tears

320
00:21:25,987 --> 00:21:28,607
as they prove our sweet snake princess's heart

321
00:21:28,607 --> 00:21:30,367
has not frozen over.

322
00:21:32,107 --> 00:21:33,327
You mock me?

323
00:21:33,607 --> 00:21:35,447
You're the one who left this nation behind!

324
00:21:35,807 --> 00:21:37,727
That's neither here nor there!

325
00:21:38,007 --> 00:21:40,827
Have you already forgotten where you would be without me?

326
00:21:41,147 --> 00:21:43,207
Yes, you escaped the celestial dragons,

327
00:21:43,207 --> 00:21:44,767
but you neglected to mention

328
00:21:44,767 --> 00:21:46,627
that you didn't know how to get home!

329
00:21:47,507 --> 00:21:48,107
Tell me,

330
00:21:48,367 --> 00:21:50,287
would you have seen Amazon Lily again

331
00:21:50,287 --> 00:21:52,027
if I hadn't gone to the outer seas?

332
00:21:52,327 --> 00:21:53,807
You would have starved to death

333
00:21:53,807 --> 00:21:55,487
hiding in the cracks of the red line

334
00:21:55,487 --> 00:21:56,807
if it wasn't for me!

335
00:21:57,127 --> 00:21:59,327
A small kindness you'll never let us forget.

336
00:21:59,587 --> 00:22:00,547
What did you say?

337
00:22:00,787 --> 00:22:01,327
Peace, Greg.

338
00:22:01,887 --> 00:22:03,707
I've watched over the three of you

339
00:22:03,707 --> 00:22:05,367
as though you were my own daughter!

340
00:22:05,447 --> 00:22:06,747
Yes, yes, we know you have.

341
00:22:06,747 --> 00:22:09,367
And you have the gold to dismiss

342
00:22:09,367 --> 00:22:10,507
all I've done for you

343
00:22:10,507 --> 00:22:11,827
as a small kindness?

344
00:22:12,367 --> 00:22:13,247
Put me down!

345
00:22:13,567 --> 00:22:13,927
Mary!

346
00:22:14,387 --> 00:22:14,947
Sonya!

347
00:22:16,127 --> 00:22:17,207
I suppose

348
00:22:17,207 --> 00:22:20,087
you find me repulsive

349
00:22:20,087 --> 00:22:21,627
now that you know I was a slave?

350
00:22:23,087 --> 00:22:23,447
Huh?

351
00:22:32,587 --> 00:22:34,767
Come on, don't tell me you're serious!

352
00:22:35,467 --> 00:22:35,907
Really?

353
00:22:35,907 --> 00:22:37,287
I told you I hate

354
00:22:37,287 --> 00:22:38,347
the celestial dragons!

355
00:22:45,987 --> 00:22:47,487
I've decided I like you.

356
00:22:48,047 --> 00:22:48,847
You said that there was

357
00:22:48,847 --> 00:22:50,407
somewhere you needed to go, yes?

358
00:22:50,847 --> 00:22:53,067
Well, my ship's at your command.

359
00:22:53,567 --> 00:22:54,287
Name the place.

360
00:22:54,487 --> 00:22:55,927
You mean it!

361
00:23:05,907 --> 00:23:07,487
I'm going to be king of the pirates!

362
00:23:07,487 --> 00:23:09,247
When the Kuja pirates hold a banquet,

363
00:23:09,247 --> 00:23:10,907
Luffy is the center of attention.

364
00:23:11,407 --> 00:23:12,487
Margaret rescues him

365
00:23:12,487 --> 00:23:13,567
from the sea of admirers

366
00:23:13,567 --> 00:23:14,927
and takes him to Granny Dione.

367
00:23:15,267 --> 00:23:16,707
She reveals troubling news

368
00:23:16,707 --> 00:23:17,647
about his brother Ace,

369
00:23:17,787 --> 00:23:19,427
and Luffy is forced to make a decision

370
00:23:19,427 --> 00:23:21,527
that will change the course of his destiny.

371
00:23:22,227 --> 00:23:22,927
On the next,

372
00:23:23,047 --> 00:23:23,607
One Piece!

373
00:23:23,947 --> 00:23:24,827
Saving Ace!

374
00:23:25,027 --> 00:23:25,767
The next stop,

375
00:23:25,867 --> 00:23:26,727
The Great Prison!

376
00:23:27,147 --> 00:23:28,907
I'm going to be king of the pirates!

377
00:23:28,907 --> 00:23:30,107
The Great Freedom!

378
00:23:30,487 --> 00:23:31,107
The Great ресPer

379
00:23:32,207 --> 00:23:32,527
Yes!

380
00:23:33,287 --> 00:23:52,247
The Great 這

